{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795608695,"nonce":"SKJklfg05m6VeWpOVOLZW2uVM4I=","title":"Overflow fade skips SVGs, and is measured from the wrong clip","message":"Two defects in `overflow-fade`:\n\n1. SVG elements ignore it. Text, shapes and RGBA draws carry the fade; `SvgElement` had no field for it, so icons at a fading edge stay solid.\n2. A shape with a clip of its own inside a fading clip fades at its own clip's edges, because the shader measures from the merged `clip_bounds` unless `clip_fade_bounds` is set, and the native paint never set it.\n\nFound while fading the rich text editor toolbar's scroll lane (26002b452b75be9fe98ed2910cd304adffc0646930cfabb9a4f22c9e719c598b).\n\nFix: collect the fading node's own box with the fade, carry both on `SvgElement`, and draw the ramp with the image instance's linear mask; set `clip_fade_bounds` where a clip inside the fading one narrows `clip_bounds`.\n\nLimits: an icon two fading edges reach takes the stronger one. Text inside a clip of its own still fades at that clip's edges, as glyphs carry no fade rect.","files":null}]}